[statement]
A name that only a package installed for its condition requires does not
narrow a decision: `a`, whose condition `d` 3 completes, needs `W`, and
both candidates for `W` are versions of `x`. apk does not take `x` 2 for
`x` and refuses, its report naming no broken constraint. Contrast
`decision-order/a-name-every-candidate-of-which-holds-another-narrows-its-choice`.

[repository]
P:a
V:1
D:W
i:d

P:d
V:3

P:x
V:3

P:x
V:2
p:W

P:x
V:1
p:W

[request]
x
d

